Magnitude of Cartesian Vectors in 3D" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051021 #edb/ref 1033 1277 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051021 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "7ab3215d-4ce4-5e76-8672-0d6b5580e957" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186067642 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186067643 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186067642 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186067644 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186067642 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186067645 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186067642 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186067646 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186067642 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186067647 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186067642 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186067642 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186067642 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "2aea7a53-b7bf-5584-8696-8766da29f419" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186067643 #edb/ref 1080 "⟨2, \\frac{1}{2}⟩" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186067643 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186067643 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c3ce49ce-6a53-5b83-9564-106f32f18abd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186067644 #edb/ref 1080 "⟨\\frac{1}{2}, \\frac{1}{2}⟩" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186067644 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186067644 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c5d8be60-3856-5e3f-b942-67b33c088ce5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186067645 #edb/ref 1080 "1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186067645 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186067645 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "ded48646-180c-5b0b-a6e9-fca073f5a695" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186067646 #edb/ref 1080 "⟨2, 2⟩" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186067646 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186067646 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f70aff19-4caa-5d25-91c6-b80e404ff000" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186067647 #edb/ref 1080 "⟨\\frac{1}{2}, 2⟩" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186067647 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186067647 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "10246158-ec52-5f5e-aaae-27da3f8bd289" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068457 #edb/ref 1069 "e-12450" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068457 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $\\mathbf r (t) = \\langle 6t, 2t^2-1\\rangle,$ calculate $\\mathbf r (3).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068457 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6eea01b2-bc2a-55a8-9bab-6789df00fc42" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068457 #edb/ref 1074 "We substitute $t=3$ into our function, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(3) & =⟨6(3),\\,2(3)^{2}-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨18,\\,17⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068458 #edb/ref 1069 "e-12451" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068458 #edb/ref 1071 "Find $\\left|\\mathbf r\\left(4\\right)\\right|$ given that $\\mathbf r(t)  = \\left\\langle 2-t, 2\\sqrt{t}, \\, t-1\\right\\rangle,$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068458 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "86e423e7-db4b-5fdf-a285-bded3bd8161e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068458 #edb/ref 1074 "Evaluating the function at $t=4,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(4) & =⟨2-4,\\,2\\sqrt{4},\\,4-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,4,\\,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the magnitude of this vector, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r(4)| & =\\sqrt{{(-2)}^{2}+{(4)}^{2}+{(3)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+16+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{29}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068459 #edb/ref 1069 "e-12452" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068459 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the value of the vector function $\\mathbf f(t) = \\left\\langle \\cos t, \\: \\sin t, \\: t \\right\\rangle$ at $t = \\pi.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068459 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ab3899d3-8838-57ad-8a17-b8ac2934c0f9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068459 #edb/ref 1074 "To evaluate, we substitute $t = \\pi$ into the function, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\pi ) & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi ,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi ,\\,\\pi ⟩=⟨-1,0,\\pi \\,⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the value of $\\mathbf f (t)$ at $t = \\pi$ is $\\langle -1, 0, \\pi \\rangle.$\n\nWe can also express the answer using $\\mathbf i$-$\\mathbf j$-$\\mathbf k$ notation or square bracket notation, as follows:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\pi \\end{aligned}]\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068857 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048293 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068857 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186069406 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068857 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186069412 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068857 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186259489 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068857 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186319272 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068857 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186319273 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068857 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345011 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068857 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345012 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068857 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345013 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068857 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186387353 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068857 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186393473 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068857 #edb/ref 1039 "Evaluating a Vector-Valued Function" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068857 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186068457 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068857 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "d59ccd52-63db-5d28-b78b-2df7caf52ad0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068858 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050988 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068858 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186051021 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068858 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186069413 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068858 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186069414 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068858 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186234368 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068858 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186259495 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068858 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186259502 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068858 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 175921